+_`<ToggleGroupItem>` gains `#media` and `#meta`, and they are what makes a set of tiles_
+
+`#media` is a row above the label (a glyph, a thumbnail, a stage), `#meta` a row below it
+(a readout, a description). A group one of whose own options fills either slot is a set
+of tiles (`--selection-tile: flush`, below): every option in it is a card, and a
+selected one carries a check in its top inline-end corner when it is at least 3.5 checks
+wide. Nothing is declared, and there is no prop. A slot that yields only a false
+`v-if`, a `v-for` over nothing or blank text is unfilled and renders no row; a child
+component counts as content whatever it renders. Wrappers between a group and its
+options (a `<section>` per family, a grid `div`) do not matter; an option belongs to its
+nearest group, so a tile group nested inside a pill group leaves the outer group pills
+and the other way round, for two levels of groups (a group three levels deep is pills).
+The silent change: a default slot that held two rows (a name over a readout) now lays
+them out on one row of a pill and clips; move the second row into `#meta` or `#media`.
